Chemical qualification follows the process stack
A formulation can perform well on a laboratory coupon yet behave differently on a patterned wafer containing copper, dielectrics, barrier metals and nanoscale features. Engineers study dissolution kinetics, selectivity, abrasive behavior and post-treatment residues in context. Qualification includes sampling across lots and equipment tools because a local process improvement should not create a downstream reliability problem.

