A lower-priced consumable may increase process defects, shorten filter service life or require additional rinses. Those changes can make total wafer costs worse even when chemical procurement looks cheaper. Commercial comparisons should link the price and purity specification to removal rate, tool availability, yield and a realistic substitution plan.

